# Review: InboxPlugin

The core is built and well tested. `runMailSync` and the `MailSyncProvider` seam are exercised end to end
by the Gmail and JMAP provider sync suites (dedup, resume after interruption, caps with `runAgain`,
cancellation, progress and canonical system tags). Tags live in the mailbox `TagIndex` and are tested;
extraction records `ExtractedFrom`; the feed cursor and its reset are tested; reply drafting in plugin-brain is
grounded on the thread and facts. Three divergences matter. The enrich cascade is the `AnalyzeMailbox` op, not
`EnrichMailbox`, and `ProcessMailbox` lives in plugin-crm as `org.dxos.operation.crm.processMailbox`; the
provider ops are defined in plugin-google and plugin-jmap under their own key namespaces rather than
`org.dxos.operation.inbox.*`. The draft-event save path is not wired: `EventArticle` passes no `onSave` and
nothing invokes `CreateGoogleCalendarEvent`, so F-5.1 and T-6 fail. The routine templates are a single daily
`analyzeMailbox` (plus a feed-triggered CRM routine), not hourly process plus daily enrich. The app graph,
deck chain and compose/send hooks have no tests; QA-1 and QA-2 are manual only.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

